## 1. Fixed algebraic coefficient divisibility (exact native caller)
Write B+ for the source B_max^+, T for the chart bicommutant, D=B_dR^+,
and t for a uniformizer of D (associated to xi). The native T contains
S and p^{-1}, and the extension fhat commutes with multiplication by T.
For a in localFieldOf Gamma (an algebraic number), theta(T) contains a:
theta(S)[1/p] is the finite local field generated by theta(Lambda),theta(z)
by Weierstrass division, and the chart hypothesis says its fixer is contained
in j(Gamma). In detail every g fixing theta(S) fixes theta(z) and theta(Lambda),
hence Lambda itself (theta injective on the finite unramified Witt ring).
Thus g fixes a. Ordinary infinite Galois correspondence places a in that
finite field. Alternatively use native mem_of_fixed_thetaPhiInvS with
K=theta(T); already the n=0 tests suffice. Inverting p in T makes the
image contain the fraction field of theta(S), a finite integral domain
over Z_p after inverting p. This is an exact algebraic field argument,
not an assertion that all of C_p lifts into T.

Let P in Q_p[X] be the minimal polynomial of a. Separability gives
G in Q_p[X] with G P' = 1 mod P by Bezout. Set F(X)=X-G(X)P(X).
Choose s_0 in T with theta(s_0)=a. Then F(a)=a, F'(a)=0, and
F(a+u)-a is divisible by u^2 as a polynomial in D[u].
Inductively s_{j+1}=F(s_j) belongs to T, and
s_j-a in t^(2^j) D. Coefficients of F are in D since p is a unit.
For every m, select j with 2^j>=m; do NOT assert that the limit lies
in T. For finitely many coefficients a_l choose t_l in T congruent
to a_l modulo t^m for each l.

Suppose L=sum_l a_l y_l belongs to t^m D, y_l in B+.
Then sum_l t_l y_l belongs to t^m D and is in B+.
Native xi_pow_dvd_iff and E associated to xi imply
sum_l t_l y_l = E^m w in B+. Apply fhat: it is T-linear, so
sum_l t_l fhat(y_l)=E^m fhat(w). Replace t_l by a_l modulo t^m D.
Consequently L'=sum_l a_l fhat(y_l) belongs to t^m D.
This holds for all m for which L is divisible; if L=0 all m apply
and separatedness gives L'=0. If L!=0 apply m=ord_t L and use the DVR.
Thus L divides L' in D. This is exactly dvd_extendToBPlus, with the
same single f and all coefficients simultaneously, including zero L.

## 2. Relation and Hodge transport at the actual valueField caller
Write i_a=phi^{-a}: A_inf -> D using the source embeddings. The field
valueField(a) is generated by the algebraic fixed field and i_a(S).
For a finite family v_l in it choose a single nonzero denominator d
from the generated subalgebra with d v_l = sum_j c_lj i_a(s_lj),
c_lj in the algebraic fixed field, s_lj in S. Finite algebraic
products expand in this form because both sets are subrings.
For r_l in A_inf, put y_lj=phi^{-a}(s_lj r_l) in B+ and
f'=phi^{-a} f phi^a on A_inf (with the codomain S included into A_inf).
This map is S-linear: phi^a(S) subset S. Apply section 1 to all (l,j).
The extension agrees with f' on A_inf, so its image on y_lj is
phi^{-a}(s_lj f(r_l)). Therefore there is u in D with
d sum_l i_a(f(r_l)) v_l = u d sum_l i_a(r_l) v_l.
Cancel d in B_dR, not by assuming d integral or a unit of D.
Every D-submodule W of B_dR containing the old sum contains the new sum.
This proves sum_map_mem_of_valueField for the same W, including W=0.

For the Hodge difference caller take x in valueField(a) intersect D.
BdRPlus.exists_Ainf_approx at n=1 gives p^m x-r in tD for a lift r
in A_inf (embedding level zero). Apply the preceding transport with
f=coord_0, coefficients (p^m x,-1), and inputs (1,phi^a r).
We get p^m x-i_a(coord_0(phi^a r)) in tD, since coord_0(1)=1.
For the Galois operators g and t_j in the actual galMonoid, tD is
stable. Their signed difference (g-1) sum_j t_j applied to this
congruence reduces to its action on one S element. The hypothesis
phi^a(E) divides (g-1) sum_j t_j s for all s in S makes that term
zero modulo tD after i_a; these Galois operators commute with phi.
Cancel p^m (a unit of D). This is the exact degree-one Hodge difference
supplier of RUN58, not a claim that every invariant scalar has an
integral lift to S at all filtration degrees.

## 3. Uniform positive-period denominators
Take nu in A_inf divisible by mu and x in B=B+[1/mu] with phi^n(x)
in Fil^{-a} for every n>=0. Clear one mu denominator:
mu^N nu^a x=b in B+. For N>0, every phi^n(b) belongs to Fil^N
since phi^n(mu), phi^n(nu) belong to Fil^1. Therefore all its
theta values vanish; the source BPlus.dvd_of_thetaBPlus_frobEnd_eq_zero
with nu=mu and mu_dvd_of_theta_frobEnd gives mu|b in B+.
Replace b by b/mu in B+ and decrease N. The filtration premise
remains attached to x, not the quotient; induction until N=0.
Thus nu^a x in B+, exactly pow_smul_mem_range_BPlus.
This retains the native simultaneous-theta divisibility reflection,
not merely divisibility at the zeroth theta.

## 4. Initial period matrix, at exists_isPeriodMatrix
Let M be a crystalline invariant basis matrix over B (invertible)
in the native basis of T. Write c0=E tau and choose v unit with
c0 v=mu. Every phi^n M is again invariant (phi commutes with Galois).
The native Hodge frame for each phi^n M gives
(phi^n M) Y_n = W_n diag(t^{k_i(n)}),
W_n in GL(D), Y_n determinant-one integral algebraic matrix
fixed by the actual group, k_i(n) in [-a,b] by the native jumps test.
The weights are not an extra bound on the Frobenius eigenvalues.
Since Y_n and its inverse have entries in D, all entries of phi^n M
lie in Fil^{-a}, and those of its inverse lie in Fil^{-b}.
Apply section 3 with nu=c0 (associated to mu) entrywise to obtain
U=c0^a M and W=c0^b M^{-1} over B+. Then U W=c0^{a+b} I.
This gives the first IsPeriodMatrix clause, without division by c0.

Both M^{-1} phi M and (phi M)^{-1} M have Galois-fixed entries
by exact cancellation of the common representation matrix.
Use the actual exists_mem_bicommutant_of_fixed (retained below)
to lift these into T, giving inverse matrices C,C^{-1} over T by
injectivity B+ -> B. Since phi(tau)=mu,
phi(c0)=phi(E)c0 v. Put F=phi(E)^a C, F'=phi(E)^{-a} C^{-1}.
The inverse phi(E) exists in T by the actual chart inverse lemma.
Then F'F=I and phi(U)=v^a U F. These give the exact Frobenius clause.
For any g fixing Lambda and theta(z), choose its lift in Gamma by
IsChartOf, and a unit r in A_inf with r g(c0)=c0 (association
of E and tau with their translates). Then the integral matrix
r^a rho(g) satisfies (r^a rho(g)) g(U)=U. This is the Galois clause.

It remains to check hat_stable, not automatic from finite height.
At n=0 the same Hodge frame yields
U Y_0 = W_0 diag(c0^a t^{k_i}).
Here c0 has t-order 1, and W_0 is integral invertible.
Thus U y divisible by E^{a+b} in B+ iff each component of Y_0^{-1}y
in D is divisible by t^{b-k_i}. Forward and backward use the exact
B+ to D reflection xi_pow_dvd_iff, since Uy lies in B+.
Each row of Y_0^{-1} has algebraic coefficients fixed by Gamma
(inverse of fixed determinant-one matrix). Section 1 with the same
f proves each row evaluation divides the row evaluation on fhat(y).
It preserves every bound b-k_i, hence U fhat(y) divisible by E^{a+b}
in B+. This is exactly the fourth IsPeriodMatrix clause. All four
clauses connect to PeriodMatrixBasis.exists_basis, then exists_frame
and FrameTheorem, then the C crystalline defect.

